# --- Page routing ---
# Every real page on this site already exists as its own .html file
# (about.html, privacy-policy.html, etc.) and is linked with that
# extension throughout the site, so no rewriting is needed for them.
#
# This rule exists purely to make sure any URL that does NOT match a
# real file (a typo, an old/guessed link, a bad crawler request, etc.)
# gets a genuine HTTP 404 response using our branded 404.html page,
# instead of silently falling back to the homepage with a 200 status.
#
# NOTE: if this site is on Cloudflare Pages, also check
# Workers & Pages > your project > Settings > Builds & deployments >
# "404 page" and make sure it's set to use 404.html and NOT
# "Single Page Application (SPA) mode" — SPA mode overrides this file
# and serves index.html for every missing route regardless.

/*  /404.html  404
